config LINUX_SUBSYS_TIME_SYNC
	tristate "Linux Subsystem Time Sync Driver"
	depends on ARM64
	default m
	help
	  This driver generates a cross-core time synchronization anchor pair
	  (cntvct_snap, wall_snap) on the Linux (big core) side and broadcasts
	  it to shared memory for RT-Thread (small core) to read, so that log
	  timestamps from both OSes can be aligned to the same wall-clock.

	  The anchor pair is generated by sandwich-reading the ARM system
	  counter (CNTVCT_EL0) and CLOCK_REALTIME, and is written to a
	  configurable reserved-memory region using seqlock semantics.

	  Say M to build this as a loadable kernel module.
